                "4325fd12d2b269f8e63ae1e698a4066dcc036a4b"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/23/89123/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                "username": "aravinths1"
            },
            "createdOn": 1775828157,
            "author": {
                "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                "username": "aravinths1"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This is incorrect.  This is the Session Priv, returned from the result of creating a new Session by posting to /SessionService/Sessions"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Updated commit message to clarify this shows session privilege, not account privilege\u2014matches the actual implementation data source."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "We already have user privilege in the User management. Do we need user privilege in the Profile settings page? Just trying to understand the use case."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, we can see privilege from User Management, but the intent here is different: Profile Settings is the user\u2019s own account page and is the most direct place for a user to verify their current effective privilege while configuring personal settings.\n\nIn User Management, users need to go to a separate module and identify their own entry; in Profile Settings it\u2019s immediately visible and contextual (next to the username), which helps reduce confusion when a feature is access-controlled and helps during troubleshooting/support (\u201cwhat privilege do I currently have?\u201d).\n\nThis change is read-only and reuses the same privilege value already available in the store\u2014no permission logic or behavior is modified."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Makes sense!\n\n\nA suggestion here:\nThrough-out the GUI, we have First word's first letter as Caps, then remaining words as lower case. \n\nHere, currently in this commit, we have `User Privilege`.\nto be uniform, we can change to `User privilege` or just `Privilege`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Just an FYI, I have proposed a rewrite of this page here:  https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/87156/2/src/views/ProfileSettings/ProfileSettings.vue\n\nI will probably abandon that PR and redo with the OpenAPI rewrite in progress."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Updated to \"Session privilege\" for consistency with style guidelines and technical accuracy\u2014this value comes from the active session, not the user account.\n\nadded this \"Session privilege\" as per this comment https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/89123/comment/84f9a136_03beb6d5/"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/ProfileSettings/ProfileSettings.vue",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This is *not* User Privilege. It is `Session` privilege."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/ProfileSettings/ProfileSettings.vue",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Fixed. Renamed both the label and local computed property to sessionPrivilege to match the data source."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/ProfileSettings/ProfileSettings.vue",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "A `<dl>` is a description list, so semantically the cleaner construction is one list with two term/description pairs:\n```\n<dl>\n  <dt>{{ $t('pageProfileSettings.username') }}</dt>\n  <dd>{{ username }}</dd>\n  <dt>{{ $t('pageProfileSettings.userPrivilege') }}</dt>\n  <dd>{{ userPrivilege }}</dd>\n</dl>\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/ProfileSettings/ProfileSettings.vue",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Consolidated to a single dl with two dt/dd pairs (Username and Session privilege).\n\n\nNote: Added this test as a regression guard for the review fixes: semantic dl structure and Session privilege labeling/value rendering, so future changes do not reintroduce the same issues."
                }
            ],
